    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "RENTER RESPONSIBILITIES AND RULES",
      "level": 2,
      "style": "SH"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "Renter must have a valid driver's license and any required boater's safety certificate or license required by state law for the Vessel type.",
        "Renter must be at least {{minimum_age}} years old and must not be intoxicated, under the influence of drugs or alcohol, or otherwise impaired while operating the Vessel.",
        "Renter is responsible for the Vessel from the time of pickup until return, including all damage, loss, theft, fines, tickets, citations, and accidents.",
        "Renter must not operate the Vessel outside of {{allowed_waters}} without Owner's written consent.",
        "Renter must not use the Vessel for any illegal purpose, racing, towing of other vehicles or persons (unless equipped and approved), jumping waves, or any dangerous or reckless operation.",
        "Renter must not allow any person not listed on the agreement to operate the Vessel.",
        "Renter must not smoke on the Vessel. Smoking damage is not covered by insurance and will be charged to Renter.",
        "Renter must not have pets on the Vessel unless approved by Owner in writing.",
        "Renter must not leave the Vessel unattended without securing it properly and removing keys.",
        "Renter must follow all Coast Guard safety regulations and state/local boating laws, including wearing a properly fitted life jacket (PFD) at all times while on the Vessel.",
        "Renter must have all required safety equipment on board (life jackets/PFDs, fire extinguisher, visual distress signals, sound-producing device, navigation lights, throwable flotation device, etc.).",
        "Renter must check weather and water conditions before and during the trip. Renter must not operate the Vessel in unsafe conditions.",
        "Renter must not exceed the Vessel's capacity (persons or weight).",
        "Renter must not anchor in prohibited areas or damage docks, moorings, buoys, or other property.",
        "Renter must report any accidents, incidents, mechanical issues, or violations to Owner immediately.",
        "Renter is responsible for environmental compliance (no dumping of waste, fuel, oil, or trash into the water).",
        "{{renter_rules_boat_extra}}"
      ]
    },
